// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO7/21 - internal power-gate lines
// (I2C_POWER/NEOPIXEL_POWER), not general-purpose. Confirmed via the
// official upstream arduino-esp32 pins_arduino.h for this exact variant
// (github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/blob/master/variants/
// adafruit_feather_esp32s3_nopsram/pins_arduino.h): `I2C_POWER`/
// `PIN_I2C_POWER` = GPIO7, `NEOPIXEL_POWER` = GPIO21 (active HIGH).
// Independently corroborated by Adafruit's own pinouts page
// (learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-esp32-s3-feather/pinouts: "You can
// manually cut power to the QT port completely by setting GPIO 7 to an
// output and LOW").
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO13 tagged "led_high" - confirmed active-high user
// LED. Adafruit's own Arduino Blink guide for this exact board
// (learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-esp32-s3-feather/arduino-blink) uses
// `digitalWrite(led, HIGH); // turn the LED on` on `LED_BUILTIN` (=
// GPIO13 per this board's pins_arduino.h and the upstream arduino-esp32
// variant file), confirming active-high polarity. NeoPixel
// (PIN_NEOPIXEL=33) NOT tagged - GPIO33 is outside the ESP32-S3
// chip-level default's available range, a pre-existing pin-availability
// gap out of scope for this tagging pass.
